IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 14.1 to 16: Undeclared Earnings Referred to in Subsection 19(3) of the
-- Act, and Deductions for Earnings or Allowances While on a Course or Program of Instruction or Training. Piece er1, layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt). Nothing here is verified against the official text. `src:N` is a line of that file.
-- Instrument: the Regulations. The Act's subsection 19(3) (piece ei1), section 61 and Part II (piece ei2), subsection 6(1), ss 7 and
-- 7.1, paragraph 59(b) are outside this piece: the facts they decide are inputs. Reg 15 was repealed (src:227).

§ `Regulation 14.1 - the end of a period to which undeclared earnings are allocated`

-- The one date this piece compares against, with its source line.
-- src:226 | 14.1 For the purpose of allocating any earnings that a claimant has failed to declare to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c), as that paragraph read immediately before August 12, 2001, where the period began before that date and was to have ended, in accordance with that paragraph, on or after that date, the period ends on August 12, 2001.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 14.1 (src:226)
`reg 14.1 August 12, 2001` MEANS YMD 2001 8 12

-- src:226 | 14.1 For the purpose of allocating any earnings that a claimant has failed to declare to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c), as that paragraph read immediately before August 12, 2001, where the period began before that date and was to have ended, in accordance with that paragraph, on or after that date, the period ends on August 12, 2001.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 14.1 (src:226)
-- Plain gloss: when earnings a claimant failed to declare are allocated to a period of the kind paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c) described
-- before August 12, 2001, a period that began before that date and was due to end on or after it ends on August 12, 2001. The answer
-- is that day; NOTHING when the period began on or after that date, or was due to end before it, because then the regulation
-- changes nothing.
GIVEN `earnings that a claimant has failed to declare are being allocated to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c), as that paragraph read immediately before August 12, 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the period was to have ended in accordance with that paragraph` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 14.1 the day on which the period ends` IS
    IF     `earnings that a claimant has failed to declare are being allocated to a period referred to in paragraph 15(4)(a), (b) or (c), as that paragraph read immediately before August 12, 2001`
       AND `the first day of the period` LESS THAN `reg 14.1 August 12, 2001`
       AND `the last day on which the period was to have ended in accordance with that paragraph` AT LEAST `reg 14.1 August 12, 2001`
    THEN JUST `reg 14.1 August 12, 2001`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:227 | 15 [Repealed, SOR/2001-291, s. 2]
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 15 (src:227)
`reg 15 repealed in this text` MEANS "reg 15: [Repealed, SOR/2001-291, s. 2]"

§ `Regulation 16 - deductions while on a course or program`

-- src:233 | (2) The allowances referred to in subsection (1) do not include
-- src:234 | (a) any amounts paid to the claimant for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or disability; or
-- src:235 | (b) in the case of work-sharing benefits, any amounts paid to the claimant using financial assistance provided under section 61 of the Act for the purpose of implementing employment support measures in respect of claimants who are entitled to work-sharing benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 16(2) (src:233-235)
-- Plain gloss: the allowances that reg 16(1) deducts leave out money paid for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or
-- disability, and (for work-sharing benefits) money paid out of assistance under section 61 of the Act (piece ei2) to carry out
-- employment support measures for claimants entitled to work-sharing benefits. The parts left out are parts of the total payable;
-- a part larger than the total is not a case the text contemplates (NOTHING).
GIVEN `the total amount of the allowances payable to the claimant for attending the course or program` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts paid to the claimant for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or disability` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant is entitled to work-sharing benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts paid to the claimant using financial assistance provided under section 61 of the Act for the purpose of implementing employment support measures in respect of claimants who are entitled to work-sharing benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 16(2) the allowances referred to in subsection (1)` IS
    IF `the allowances left after the amounts reg 16(2) excludes` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST `the allowances left after the amounts reg 16(2) excludes`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the allowances left after the amounts reg 16(2) excludes` MEANS
              `the total amount of the allowances payable to the claimant for attending the course or program`
            MINUS `the amounts paid to the claimant for dependant care, travel, commuting, living away from home or disability`
            MINUS (IF `the claimant is entitled to work-sharing benefits`
                   THEN `the amounts paid to the claimant using financial assistance provided under section 61 of the Act for the purpose of implementing employment support measures in respect of claimants who are entitled to work-sharing benefits`
                   ELSE 0)

-- src:230 | 16 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an amount equal to the total amount of any allowances payable to a claimant for attending a course or program of instruction or training, other than a course or program to which the Commission or an authority designated by the Commission has referred the claimant, shall be deducted from the benefits payable to the claimant in respect of any week of unemployment
-- src:231 | (a) during which the claimant is attending the course or program; and
-- src:232 | (b) for which the allowances are payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 16(1) (src:230-232)
-- Plain gloss: for a week in which the claimant attends a course or program (not one the Commission, or an authority it designated,
-- referred them to) and allowances are payable for that week, the benefits for that week are reduced by the allowances, as reg 16(2)
-- defines them. The answer is the amount deducted; NOTHING when the week does not meet (a) and (b), or the course was a referred one.
GIVEN `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is attending the course or program during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowances are payable for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission or an authority designated by the Commission has referred the claimant to the course or program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowances referred to in subsection (1), as reg 16(2) defines them` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 16(1) the amount deducted from the benefits for a week of unemployment while attending a course or program` IS
    IF     `the week is a week of unemployment`
       AND `the claimant is attending the course or program during the week`
       AND `the allowances are payable for the week`
       AND NOT (`the Commission or an authority designated by the Commission has referred the claimant to the course or program`)
    THEN `the allowances referred to in subsection (1), as reg 16(2) defines them`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:236 | (3) The total amount of the earnings and allowances paid under Part II of the Act shall be deducted from the benefits payable to a claimant in respect of those weeks where the claimant
-- src:237 | (a) does not meet the qualifying conditions of section 7 or 7.1 of the Act or of any regulations made under Part VIII of the Act, or is disentitled or disqualified within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act;
-- src:238 | (b) is paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for certain weeks for attending a course or program of instruction or training or is paid earnings from employment for certain weeks of employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects; and
-- src:239 | (c) subsequently becomes entitled to regular benefits in respect of the same weeks as those for which the amounts under paragraph (b) were paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 16(3) (src:236-239)
-- Plain gloss: if a claimant is paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for weeks of a course, or earnings from an employment
-- support measure that gives work experience, for weeks when they did not qualify for (or were disentitled or disqualified from)
-- benefits, and later become entitled to regular benefits for those same weeks, the whole of what was paid under Part II is deducted from
-- the benefits for those weeks. The answer is the amount deducted; NOTHING when (a), (b) or (c) is not met.
GIVEN `the claimant does not meet the qualifying conditions of section 7 or 7.1 of the Act or of any regulations made under Part VIII of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is disentitled within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is disqualified within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for certain weeks for attending a course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is paid earnings from employment for certain weeks of employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant subsequently becomes entitled to regular benefits in respect of the same weeks as those for which the amounts under paragraph (b) were paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total amount of the earnings and allowances paid under Part II of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 16(3) the amount deducted from the benefits for the weeks for which Part II earnings or allowances were paid` IS
    IF     (   `the claimant does not meet the qualifying conditions of section 7 or 7.1 of the Act or of any regulations made under Part VIII of the Act`
            OR `the claimant is disentitled within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act`
            OR `the claimant is disqualified within the meaning of subsection 6(1) of the Act`)
       AND (   `the claimant is paid earnings or allowances under Part II of the Act for certain weeks for attending a course or program of instruction or training`
            OR `the claimant is paid earnings from employment for certain weeks of employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act that is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`)
       AND `the claimant subsequently becomes entitled to regular benefits in respect of the same weeks as those for which the amounts under paragraph (b) were paid`
    THEN JUST `the total amount of the earnings and allowances paid under Part II of the Act`
    ELSE NOTHING
